# =============================================================================
# CRUCIBLE — .gitignore
# =============================================================================
# This file enforces the single most important opsec rule of an offensive
# engagement: nothing that could compromise a target, expose a victim, or
# burn an operator ever leaves the host it was generated on.
#
# Three classes of artifact must NEVER be committed:
#
#   1.  LOOT       — anything obtained from the target. Credentials, tokens,
#                    session cookies, dumped data, exfil samples. Even one
#                    leaked record is a breach. Treat loot/ as radioactive.
#
#   2.  EVIDENCE   — request/response pairs, screenshots, recordings,
#                    network captures. These contain target hostnames,
#                    internal IPs, employee names, headers, sometimes
#                    cookies. They are NOT for public consumption.
#
#   3.  IDENTITY   — operator credentials, infra keys, C2 configs, VPN
#                    profiles. Compromise here means the next engagement
#                    starts already burned.
#
# The framework/ tree itself is shareable. The targets/ tree is not.
# When in doubt, do not commit. Add it here, then commit the .gitignore.
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-engagement working data — these directories live under targets/<name>/
# and contain everything that could possibly identify, expose, or harm a
# real target. We ignore them by pattern so a freshly-cloned repo gets the
# template scaffolding but never inherits another engagement's artifacts.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
targets/*/loot/**
targets/*/evidence/**
targets/*/recon/raw/**
targets/*/recon/**/*.json
targets/*/recon/**/*.xml
targets/*/recon/**/*.txt
targets/*/recon/**/*.csv
targets/*/recon/**/*.html
targets/*/recon/**/screenshots/
targets/*/source/**

# Findings and reports often contain sanitized but still-sensitive material
# (CVEs scoped to a private codebase, internal endpoint names, hash samples).
# Block the populated outputs but keep the README scaffolding visible.
targets/*/findings/FINDING-*.md
targets/*/findings/CHAIN-*.md
targets/*/reports/*.pdf
targets/*/reports/*.docx
targets/*/reports/draft-*.md
targets/*/reports/final-*.md

# Engagement notes contain raw working memory — hypotheses tested, payloads
# tried, dead ends, dialogue with the client. Sensitive by default.
targets/*/notes/command-log.md
targets/*/notes/engagement-log.md
targets/*/notes/endpoints.md
targets/*/notes/role-matrix.md
targets/*/notes/test-artifacts.md
targets/*/notes/hypotheses.md

# Signed charter pages contain wet signatures, government IDs, real names,
# legal entity addresses. These NEVER leave the engagement folder.
targets/*/charter-signed.pdf
targets/*/charter-signed.png
targets/*/charter-signed-*.pdf
targets/*/authorization-letter.pdf
targets/*/get-out-of-jail.pdf

# The _template directory IS supposed to ship — its files are scaffolding,
# not data. Whitelist the template explicitly so the patterns above don't
# strip it.
!targets/_template/
!targets/_template/**

# Per-target README.md, charter.md, threat-model.md, attack-tree.md are
# the entry points for the engagement and should usually be tracked
# (sanitized scope is fine to commit). Anything more sensitive than that
# goes in the directories blocked above. Whitelist these explicitly:
!targets/*/README.md
!targets/*/charter.md
!targets/*/threat-model.md
!targets/*/attack-tree.md
!targets/*/recon/README.md
!targets/*/findings/README.md
!targets/*/evidence/README.md
!targets/*/loot/README.md
!targets/*/reports/README.md
!targets/*/notes/README.md


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials, keys, secrets — anywhere in the tree, no exceptions.
# These patterns are deliberately broad. False positives are recoverable;
# a leaked private key is not.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.pkcs12
*.jks
*.keystore
*.crt
*.csr
*.cer
*.der
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*
id_ecdsa
id_ecdsa.*
*_rsa
*_ed25519
*_ecdsa
known_hosts
authorized_keys

# Secret-bearing config files
.env
.env.*
*.env
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
secrets.json
secrets.toml
credentials
credentials.*
*credentials*.json
*credentials*.yaml
*credentials*.yml
.netrc
.pgpass
.aws/
.azure/
.gcloud/
gcloud-key.json
service-account*.json
firebase-adminsdk*.json

# Cookie jars, session files, token caches
cookies.txt
cookies.jar
*.cookies
session.json
sessions/
tokens.json
*.token
.bearer
authn-cache/


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tool output — wordlists, scan results, intermediate caches. These are
# generated, not authored, and frequently contain target-identifying data.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
framework/wordlists/*.txt
framework/wordlists/*.lst
framework/wordlists/SecLists/
framework/wordlists/PayloadsAllTheThings/
framework/wordlists/seclists/
framework/wordlists/cache/

# Local installs of tooling — don't pollute the repo with binaries
framework/tools/bin/
framework/tools/opt/
framework/tools/.cache/
framework/tools/go/
framework/tools/venv/
framework/tools/node_modules/

# Common scanner output formats anywhere in the tree
*.nessus
*.nmap
*.gnmap
*.xml.bak
nuclei-output/
ffuf-output/
gobuster-output/
amass-output/
subfinder-output/
httpx-output/
zap-report.*
burp-state.*
*.burpstate

# Recon raw dumps anywhere — belt and braces with the targets/ rules
**/recon-raw/
**/raw-dumps/
**/breach-data/
**/dehashed/
**/intelx/
**/leakcheck/


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Standard development noise — Python, Node, OS, editors. Listed last
# because the security-relevant entries above are what actually matter.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

